{
  "abstract": "Unconditional Lean 4 + Mathlib formalization of Carmichael's totient conjecture lower-bound and density-transfer theory (zero sorry, zero native_decide, standard axioms only): proves 10^10,117 < x unconditionally for every Carmichael counterexample x (10^10,240 < x in Case I and 10^10,117 < x in Case II via 161 kernel-checked Lucas primality ladders, surpassing Masai and Valette's 1982 bound of 10^10,000), the unconditional pure-kernel limiting singleton density bound liminf V1(X)/V(X) < 10^-5,057, totient-value and density transfer via Ford's (1998) Lemmas 7.4-7.5 and Chebyshev's prime lower bound, Ford's Lemma 7.2 prime-square forcing rule, Klee's (1947) minimal-counterexample structure, Pomerance's (1974) sufficient condition, Ford's reduction to k = 6, and the unconditional bound m >= 32,000 for Ford's k = 10 divisible-preimage problem, plus non-vacuity witnesses. Scope note: the larger 10^100,000,160,994 Carmichael bound, 10^-50,000,080,497 density bound, and m >= 10^60 k = 10 bound in the companion manuscript (https://mathdiscoveries.org/results/carmichael-totient) rely on external exact-integer certificates whose soundness and transfer theorems are proved in this library.",
